op"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;2,308.5&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000;border-top:0.25pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000;border-top:0.25pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;22.5&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000;border-top:0.25pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;%&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:5pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:5pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On December 22, 2017, the Tax Cuts and Jobs Act (TCJA) was signed into law. For businesses, the legislation reduced the corporate federal tax rate from a maximum of 35% to 21%, effective January 1, 2018. In addition, UPPCO recorded a regulatory liability related to the remeasurement of its utility deferred taxes in the amount of $6,358.5 thousand as of December 31, 2017. This net regulatory liability is amortizing as discussed in Note 13, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Regulatory Environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The deferred income tax assets included on the balance sheets as of December 31, 2025, and 2024, are primarily related to tax basis goodwill and net operating losses. The principal deferred income tax liabilities included on the balance sheets as of December 31, 2025, and 2024 are primarily related to employee benefits and plant.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The table below details the deferred tax balances as of December 31, 2025, and 2024:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:10pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:center"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:84.970%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:58.444%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.740%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.516%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;(Thousands)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri',sans-serif;font-size:9.5pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;